---
layout: none
permalink: /wire/cves.xml
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{%- comment -%}
  The Wire's CVEs tab (T-0522) as an Atom feed: one entry per CVE the exporter's selection
  rule lists (significant, recent, not yet on a KEV list, with a public exploit, a public
  rule or a high EPSS percentile), from the same `cves:` rows /wire/ renders (_data/wire.yml,
  written by wire_export.py). Each entry links to its row on /wire/. Modelled on vulns.xml:
  data fields only, no description, and nothing from cve.now's model-written summaries.
  Metasploit and Exploit-DB entries are claimed only when confirmed against their publishers' indexes.
  Without CVE data this is a valid, empty feed rather than a 404.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign wire = site.data.wire %}
{%- assign sev_bands = "critical,high,medium,low" | split: "," %}
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
  <title>{{ site.title | xml_escape }}: The Wire, CVEs (significant new CVEs not yet on a KEV list)</title>
  <subtitle>This feed is my selection of new CVEs with a critical flaw in a product CISA has listed before, a confirmed public exploit or a high EPSS percentile, that are not on VulnCheck KEV or CISA KEV. Being listed does not mean exploitation has been seen. Facts come from cve.now (CC BY 4.0), CISA SSVC through Vulnrichment, FIRST EPSS, Exploit-DB and Metasploit.</subtitle>
  <link href="{{ site.url }}/wire/cves.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/>
  <link href="{{ site.url }}/wire/#cves" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
  <link href="https://cve.now/" rel="via" type="text/html" title="cve.now"/>
  <updated>{% if wire and wire.cves_generated_at and wire.cves_generated_at != "" %}{{ wire.cves_generated_at | date_to_xmlschema }}{% elsif wire and wire.generated_at %}{{ wire.generated_at | date_to_xmlschema }}{% else %}{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}{% endif %}</updated>
  <id>{{ site.url }}/wire/cves.xml</id>
  <author>
    <name>{{ site.title | xml_escape }}</name>
    <uri>{{ site.url }}/wire/#cves</uri>
  </author>
  <rights>Data from cve.now (CC BY 4.0), CISA Vulnrichment, FIRST EPSS, Exploit-DB and the Metasploit Framework. Selection by {{ site.title | xml_escape }}.</rights>
{%- if wire and wire.cves and wire.cves != empty %}
  {%- if wire.cves_status == "ok" or wire.cves_status == "stale" %}
  {%- for r in wire.cves limit: 500 %}
  {%- comment %} The page's row guard: an empty string is true in Liquid, so check shapes. {% endcomment %}
  {%- assign cve_head = r.cve | slice: 0, 4 %}{% assign pub_len = r.published | size %}
  {%- if cve_head == "CVE-" and pub_len == 10 %}
  {%- assign vday = r.published %}
  {%- include wire-cve-why.html %}
  {%- assign msf_len = r.msf | size %}{% assign edb_len = r.edb | size %}
  <entry>
    <title>{{ r.cve | xml_escape }}{% if r.vendor and r.vendor != "" %}: {{ r.vendor | xml_escape }} {{ r.product | xml_escape }}{% endif %}</title>
    <link href="{{ site.url }}/wire/#cves-{{ r.cve | downcase | xml_escape }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/{{ r.cve | xml_escape }}" rel="related" type="text/html" title="NVD"/>
    <link href="https://cve.now/{{ r.cve | xml_escape }}" rel="related" type="text/html" title="cve.now"/>
    {%- comment %} Metasploit modules and Exploit-DB entries are linked as the Exploits popover links them. {% endcomment %}
    {%- for m in r.msf %}
    <link href="https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/blob/master/{{ m | uri_escape | xml_escape }}" rel="related" type="text/html" title="Metasploit module"/>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- for e in r.edb %}
    <link href="https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/{{ e | uri_escape | xml_escape }}" rel="related" type="text/html" title="Exploit-DB entry"/>
    {%- endfor %}
    <id>{{ site.url }}/wire/#cves-{{ r.cve | downcase | xml_escape }}</id>
    <published>{{ vday | xml_escape }}T00:00:00Z</published>
    <updated>{{ vday | xml_escape }}T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <category term="cves-tab" label="CVEs tab"/>
    {%- if w_ab %}
    <category term="critical-no-login-kev-product" label="Critical, no login needed, product on CISA KEV"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if w_epss %}
    <category term="epss-top-10" label="EPSS top 10%"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if msf_len > 0 %}
    <category term="metasploit-module" label="Metasploit module"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if edb_len > 0 %}
    <category term="exploit-db" label="Exploit-DB entry"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- assign n_sids = r.et_sids | size %}
    {%- if n_sids > 0 %}
    <category term="et-open-rule" label="ET Open rule"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- assign nu_len = r.nuclei | size %}
    {%- if nu_len > 0 %}
    <category term="nuclei-template" label="Nuclei template"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- assign cvss_len = r.cvss | size %}
    {%- assign sev = "" %}
    {%- if cvss_len > 0 %}{% if sev_bands contains r.severity %}{% assign sev = r.severity %}{% endif %}{% endif %}
    {%- if sev != "" %}
    <category term="severity-{{ r.severity | xml_escape }}" label="CVSS {{ r.severity | upcase | xml_escape }} {{ r.cvss | xml_escape }}"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- assign epss_len = r.epss | append: "" | size %}
    <summary type="text">Published {{ vday | xml_escape }}{% if sev != "" %}; CVSS v{{ r.cvss_version | xml_escape }} {{ r.cvss | xml_escape }} {{ r.severity | upcase | xml_escape }}, scored by {% if r.scored_by == "cve.now" %}cve.now (no score in our NVD data){% else %}{% if r.scored_by == "NVD" %}NVD{% elsif r.scored_by == "ADP" %}CISA's ADP{% else %}the CNA{% endif %} (VulnCheck NVD++){% endif %}{% endif %}{% if epss_len > 0 %}; EPSS {{ r.epss | times: 1.0 | round: 3 }}{% endif %}{% if w_ab %}; Critical and reachable with no login, in a product on CISA KEV ({{ kn }} before; a fact about the product, not this CVE){% endif %}{% if w_epss %}; EPSS top 10%{% endif %}{% if msf_len > 0 %}; {{ msf_len }} Metasploit module{% if msf_len != 1 %}s{% endif %} (confirmed){% endif %}{% if edb_len > 0 %}; {{ edb_len }} Exploit-DB entr{% if edb_len == 1 %}y{% else %}ies{% endif %} (confirmed){% endif %}. Not in a KEV list when selected; exploitation not implied.</summary>
  </entry>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
</feed>
